		<div class="topic" id="forum_op_topic_572679173080109213">
		I hope we start getting LESS AI-slop devs.	</div>
	<div class="content" id="forum_op_content_572679173080109213">
		That this &quot;dev&quot; already is pumping out their third AI-slop title is frightening. If nothing changes soon, we won't be able to sift through all the trash being dumped on the store.	</div>
		
	<div class="forum_op_footer">
		<div></div>
			</div>
</div>
<div data-featuretarget="community-awards"></div>
<script type="text/javascript">
	$J( function() {
		InitializeForumTopic( {"owner":"46277277","type":"General","feature":"0","gidforum":"590692129307765155","forum_display_name":"General Discussions","forum_url":"https:\/\/steamcommunity.com\/app\/5103870\/discussions\/0\/","forum_search_url":"https:\/\/steamcommunity.com\/app\/5103870\/discussions\/search\/","is_public":1,"permissions":{"can_view":1,"can_post":1,"can_reply":1,"is_banned":0,"can_delete":0,"can_edit":0},"appid":5103870}, "https:\/\/steamcommunity.com\/forum\/46277277\/General\/",
		"572679173080109213", {"author":"Painfully Unmagic","text":"That this \"dev\" already is pumping out their third AI-slop title is frightening. If nothing changes soon, we won't be able to sift through all the trash being dumped on the store."}		);
			} );
</script>
										<script type="text/javascript">
$J( function() { InitializeCommentThread( "ForumTopic", "ForumTopic_103582791475798685_590692129307765155_572679173080109213", {"feature":"590692129307765155","feature2":"572679173080109213","owner":"103582791475798685","commentthreadid":"661981946","total_count":31,"start":0,"pagesize":15,"has_upvoted":0,"upvotes":0,"votecountid":null,"voteupid":null,"commentcountid":null,"subscribed":false,"extended_data":"{\"topic_permissions\":{\"can_view\":1,\"can_post\":1,\"can_reply\":1,\"is_banned\":0,\"can_delete\":0,\"can_edit\":0},\"original_poster\":47928107,\"topic_gidanswer\":\"0\",\"forum_appid\":5103870,\"forum_public\":1,\"forum_type\":\"General\",\"forum_gidfeature\":\"0\"}","oldestfirst":true,"comments_raw":{"572679173080114519":{"text":"3 out of 4 of my games were released before AI could code at all. And, AI Roguelite released even before ChatGPT was invented.\n\nSo this game is my first \"AI slop\" game if you want to call it that, and it is far more polished than the stuff I could make in the same amount of time, so I don't think it's realistic to hope less people use it.","author":"AI Roguelite: AI-generated RPG"},"572679173080115794":{"text":"[quote=Painfully Unmagic]That this \"dev\" already is pumping out their third AI-slop title is frightening. If nothing changes soon, we won't be able to sift through all the trash being dumped on the store. [\/quote]\nSeems unfair.","author":"PeaceMaker"},"572679173080117140":{"text":"Your numbers are slightly off, Anywhere RPG is the fourth title by the dev. That said, it maybe makes more sense to consider it one large project to explore the capabilities of AI for emergent gameplay. As the capabilities grow, there is more potential to explore another approach, and some of those work better, some worse.\n\nI agree that there is a problem with low-effort AI products flooding the market and taking opportunity away from artists and other creators, but I think you are judging this one somewhat incorrectly, as creating frameworks that utilize AI as core functionality is pretty distinct from anything else we have seen in game development in the past, and much different from simply vibe-coding or asset generating a fixed experience.\n\nIf you wish for more perspective, across all of his titles the dev offers a free service to run his AI models to power the game, at his own cost, mostly without limits, which includes the risk that some buyers might eventually cost him more money than he made by selling the game to them. I think the mark of \"slop\" is trying to cut corners and make quick income, while this one is closer to an indie passion project that chases an elusive vision and wants to share it with some people on the way.","author":"Nathan Pascal"},"572679173080117221":{"text":"This game is way more fun than most non-AI games, even AAA with millions $ budget.\n\nThanks DEV.","author":"Gina"},"572679173080117280":{"text":"[quote=Painfully Unmagic]That this \"dev\" already is pumping out their third AI-slop title is frightening. If nothing changes soon, we won't be able to sift through all the trash being dumped on the store. [\/quote]\n\nGames that use AI != AI slop.\n\nAs they already said, they released titles before AI could even code, the core of this game is having an AI gamemaster similar to titles like AIdventure or AI2U.\n\nThe fact is that this game is doing something unique in the space. At worst, it's a minimum viable product or tech demo, which is fine for Early Access. AI slop is any one of the dozen needle in a haystack games.","author":"Tydorius"},"572679173080117383":{"text":"Too be fair this is one of the first proper uses of AI I have seen so far, it may be rough around the edges, but in comparison to other uses in other areas of AI, this one sits well, instead of it just writing a story, it's more like a interactive show, and depending on the model you use it could easily alter however you want to play it out.\n\nAside from that, it is getting old with people blindly attacking AI, its here, and theres pretty much nothing anyone can do about it, aside from that its just the same garbage complaints you found before AI, just a situation of \"Same thing different beef\", waste of everyones time.\n\nAnyways, if your going to throw hate, throw it at stuff that actually deserves it, and if you wonder what that is, use some common sense.\n\nAs a hint, if this game were given too a number of writers, and told to make x number of creations, how well do you think they would do it? would it even ever get done? this game is near infinite in what can be made, if your crying because you think it is best left to humans, you failed to realize it would never be finished, therefore good use for the tool used, its incapable of being human created therefore it shouldnt be expected to be, thats more immoral then the actual use of the tool may feel, due to how much effort they would have to put, and knowing that they likely would have to do this every day for the rest of there life.","author":"\u043do\u0442\u0440i\u0438\u043a"},"572679173080156587":{"text":"This game is amazing I can literally do anything and watch the world react. Its like a dream simulator I love it thank you oh mighty dev !! <3","author":"Ara Ara"},"572679490124120941":{"text":"[quote=\u043do\u0442\u0440i\u0438\u043a;572679173080117383]\n\nAside from that, it is getting old with people blindly attacking AI, its here, and theres pretty much nothing anyone can do about it, aside from that its just the same garbage complaints you found before AI, just a situation of \"Same thing different beef\", waste of everyones time.\n\n[\/quote]\n\nYea that bugs me too. I do see potential problems with over-reaching AI in the REAL world and I'm against that, but one should see where it is a useful TOOL too. Now in games especially use it right and it will be amazing. Anywhere RPG is going in the right direction for games, in fact, exactly as I'd hoped. An AI GM where no human GM might be available - and it works quite well.\n\nThis blatantly attacking AI cos `AI` is dumb and I think some people just leap on the bamdwagon without thought cos it's fashionable. Use discernment. AI is fine if used as a TOOL to make better games.","author":"PeaceMaker"},"572679490124121887":{"text":"The developer creates amazing games. Your complaints are unfounded.","author":"litdanser"},"572679490124124721":{"text":"The game is magnificent; the AI \u200b\u200bis perfectly integrated and offers tremendous replayability. Kudos to the creator.","author":"NekitaS"},"572679490124126541":{"text":"Though since the 0.18 (it would be nice what are the changes between each version) the AI generation of variables does not obey anymore apparently.\na Shame.","author":"Buchanan"},"572679490124149401":{"text":"This game is an AI gem, I played the demo and it was great. Hopefully it gets more developed.","author":"Brigadoom"},"572679490124152273":{"text":"[quote=Painfully Unmagic]That this \"dev\" already is pumping out their third AI-slop title is frightening. If nothing changes soon, we won't be able to sift through all the trash being dumped on the store. [\/quote]\n\n50 points have been deposited in your social credit account","author":"Flauxhawk"},"572679490124152664":{"text":"The irony is that GAMERS are complaining about AI RUN GAMES in a world where GAME AI used to be a huge selling point.","author":"Ciecieji"},"572679490124157170":{"text":"[quote=Ciecieji;572679490124152664]The irony is that GAMERS are complaining about AI RUN GAMES in a world where GAME AI used to be a huge selling point. [\/quote]\n\nIt is ironic. On another forum everyone complains about bad `AI` before but when I say well with real AI we might actually get a decent game they all start wailing they don't actually want an AI, they just want `something`.","author":"PeaceMaker"}},"track_navigation":true}, 'https://steamcommunity.com/comment/ForumTopic/', 40 ); } );
</script>
<div class="commentthread_area forumtopic_comments" id="commentthread_ForumTopic_103582791475798685_590692129307765155_572679173080109213_area">
	        <div id="commentthread_ForumTopic_103582791475798685_590692129307765155_572679173080109213_pagectn" class="forum_paging" style="">
