				</div>

				
				<div class="commentthread_comment_actions" >
														<a class="forum_comment_action forum_comment_action_trigger" data-tooltip-type="selector" data-tooltip-content="#forum_comment_actions_menu_572679173080117383">
					<span><i class="ico16 arrow_down"></i></span>
				</a>
			
			<div class="forum_comment_action_menu" style="display: none;" id="forum_comment_actions_menu_572679173080117383">				<a class="forum_comment_action report tooltip" href="javascript:Forum_ShowReportDialog( '103582791475798685', '590692129307765155', '572679173080109213', '16413507', '572679173080117383' );" data-tooltip-text="Report this post for inappropriate content.  Reported post are flagged for review by moderators.">
				<span class="non_breaking_space">&nbsp;</span><img src="https://community.akamai.steamstatic.com/public/images/skin_1/notification_icon_flag_dark.png?v=1">Report this post</a>
			</div>
							</div>
			</div>
			<div class="commentthread_comment_text" id="comment_content_572679173080117383">
				Too be fair this is one of the first proper uses of AI I have seen so far, it may be rough around the edges, but in comparison to other uses in other areas of AI, this one sits well, instead of it just writing a story, it's more like a interactive show, and depending on the model you use it could easily alter however you want to play it out.<br><br>Aside from that, it is getting old with people blindly attacking AI, its here, and theres pretty much nothing anyone can do about it, aside from that its just the same garbage complaints you found before AI, just a situation of &quot;Same thing different beef&quot;, waste of everyones time.<br><br>Anyways, if your going to throw hate, throw it at stuff that actually deserves it, and if you wonder what that is, use some common sense.<br><br>As a hint, if this game were given too a number of writers, and told to make x number of creations, how well do you think they would do it? would it even ever get done? this game is near infinite in what can be made, if your crying because you think it is best left to humans, you failed to realize it would never be finished, therefore good use for the tool used, its incapable of being human created therefore it shouldnt be expected to be, thats more immoral then the actual use of the tool may feel, due to how much effort they would have to put, and knowing that they likely would have to do this every day for the rest of there life.			</div>
			<div class="comment_footer_ctn">
