				</a>
			
			<div class="forum_comment_action_menu" style="display: none;" id="forum_comment_actions_menu_572679490124120941">				<a class="forum_comment_action report tooltip" href="javascript:Forum_ShowReportDialog( '103582791475798685', '590692129307765155', '572679173080109213', '17179259', '572679490124120941' );" data-tooltip-text="Report this post for inappropriate content.  Reported post are flagged for review by moderators.">
				<span class="non_breaking_space">&nbsp;</span><img src="https://community.akamai.steamstatic.com/public/images/skin_1/notification_icon_flag_dark.png?v=1">Report this post</a>
			</div>
							</div>
			</div>
			<div class="commentthread_comment_text" id="comment_content_572679490124120941">
				<blockquote class="bb_blockquote with_author"><div class="bb_quoteauthor">Originally posted by <b><a href="#c572679173080117383">нoтрiик</a></b>:</div><br>Aside from that, it is getting old with people blindly attacking AI, its here, and theres pretty much nothing anyone can do about it, aside from that its just the same garbage complaints you found before AI, just a situation of &quot;Same thing different beef&quot;, waste of everyones time.</blockquote><br>Yea that bugs me too. I do see potential problems with over-reaching AI in the REAL world and I'm against that, but one should see where it is a useful TOOL too. Now in games especially use it right and it will be amazing. Anywhere RPG is going in the right direction for games, in fact, exactly as I'd hoped. An AI GM where no human GM might be available - and it works quite well.<br><br>This blatantly attacking AI cos `AI` is dumb and I think some people just leap on the bamdwagon without thought cos it's fashionable. Use discernment. AI is fine if used as a TOOL to make better games.			</div>
			<div class="comment_footer_ctn">
									<div></div>
				
				
